{
 "format": "damap",
 "version": 1,
 "id": "99b",
 "name": "Yvhh La'tami and Snaer Hafwa Hunting Area",
 "file": "Map99b_Snaer_Yvhh_Hunting_Area.xml",
 "rooms": [
  {"id":1,"x":20,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Hemlock Forest","descriptions":["Young saplings crowd the undergrowth of the forest and create a dense mesh of vegetation impenetrable except where the trail forces its way through.  No animal, or even insect life, stirs about.  The only sound is the lulling whisper of hemlock needles as the branches sway in gentle winds high overhead."],"exits":[{"to":4,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":2,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":2,"x":20,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Hemlock Forest","descriptions":["The ground holds puddles of water even in dry weather, where runoff has collected and stagnated.  The hemlock needles float in the shallow, brackish water, hiding it until the gentle splash of a footfall reveals the soggy earth.  The trees crowd close to the trail, allowing only a narrow passage through."],"exits":[{"to":1,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":3,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":3,"x":20,"y":100,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Woodland Path","descriptions":["The thick tangle of hemlocks thins upon the approach to a clearing at the top of the path's rise.  Within the clearing is a cluster of small buildings, although it is difficult to determine much about them from this point.  Another very narrow trail threads its way over a fallen and rotting trunk straight north, but the encroaching trees quickly hide its destination."],"exits":[{"to":0,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":0,"exit":"west","move":"west"}],"linksTo":"Map99_Aesry_Town.xml"},
  {"id":4,"x":20,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Hemlock Forest","descriptions":["A shallow ditch cuts across the path and runs along beside the trail a short distance until it plunges out of sight into the forest growth to the west.  This gully, dug by rainfall and melting snows, channels its way to the lake below, and puddles remain on the saturated ground even in dry weather."],"exits":[{"to":5,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":1,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":5,"x":40,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Hemlock Forest","descriptions":["In the shadow of the steep cliff rising to the north, the hemlocks grow close together, their branches entwined and woven in a matted mass of snarls.  The sky is barely visible overhead and it is a startling moment when a glimmer of starlight manages to penetrate the net of boughs.  The distant sound of tumbling rocks ricochets dully off the cliff face high overhead where something struggles in the dark."],"exits":[{"to":6,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":4,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":6,"x":40,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Hemlock Forest","descriptions":["The narrow trail plunges on into the dense trees, weaving amongst the scented, drooping branches.  The smaller trees show scars where the bark was stripped away, either by a gnawing animal, or cut and harvested for medicinal uses."],"exits":[{"to":7,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":5,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":7,"x":60,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Bottom of Cliff","descriptions":["A cliff rises overhead as the northeastern slope of the island sweeps upwards at an impossible angle.  The initial climb up is a mixture of earth and protruding rocks, but not far overhead is a broken face of red-veined dark stone.  Hemlock trees crowd right to the base of the cliff, a few smaller specimens even encroaching up the lower reaches of the ascent."],"exits":[{"to":6,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":8,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rock ledge"}]},
  {"id":8,"x":80,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Cliff","descriptions":["This ledge is just high enough to see over the hemlock forest below and beyond to the far side of the lake.  Gusts of wind sweep across the tops of the trees, appearing for all the world like a sea of silvery green waves shifting and swelling.  A thin ledge overhead is accessible by the protruding roots in the soil and cracks in the projecting rocks that may serve as handholds."],"exits":[{"to":9,"exit":"climb","move":"climb thin ledge"},{"to":7,"exit":"climb","move":"climb down"}]},
  {"id":9,"x":100,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Cliff","descriptions":["This long thin ledge provides little room for movement.  A flat rock juts out overhead and another ledge appears within reach below -- either option seems safer than lingering here.  A scuttering sound scratches over the rocks as some unseen creature darts safely out of sight."],"exits":[{"to":8,"exit":"climb","move":"climb lower ledge"},{"to":10,"exit":"climb","move":"climb jutting rock"}]},
  {"id":10,"x":120,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Cliff","descriptions":["A huge dark rock juts out from the cliff face and offers a comfortable resting point before continuing to climb.  A clump of burr-weeds grows from a crevice and thrashes against the hard surface of the rock with a raspy whisper as the wind whips across the cliff."],"exits":[{"to":11,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":9,"exit":"climb","move":"climb thin ledge"}]},
  {"id":11,"x":120,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Cliff","descriptions":["At the juncture of the rock and the cliff, long cracks mar the vertical face.  Some of these cracks are almost wide enough to squeeze into, but the weather has created enough chinks to assist a climb up to another rocky perch above.  A constant drip, drip comes from somewhere within the cracks."],"exits":[{"to":10,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":12,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rock perch"}]},
  {"id":12,"x":120,"y":-120,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, A High Perch","descriptions":["Deep vertical cracks, like gashed wounds, continue up and down the cliff face.  This perch offers little protection from the wind and weather that can pound against the cliff wall.  Bits of rock crumble and fall with each movement -- at this height, the climb is not one for the inexperienced.  A rock shelf is visible even higher above."],"exits":[{"to":13,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rock shelf"},{"to":11,"exit":"climb","move":"climb down"}]},
  {"id":13,"x":120,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Cliff","descriptions":["Barely a third of the way up the cliff, this shelf cut from the rock is wide enough to comfortably pause upon.  Scraggly bushes, leafless with wooly stems, cling to every crack deep enough to hold a spoonful of sandy soil.  A long horizontal crevice slices through the rock overhead, and appears to be deep enough to crawl inside."],"exits":[{"to":14,"exit":"climb","move":"climb narrow crevice"},{"to":12,"exit":"climb","move":"climb rock shelf"}]},
  {"id":14,"x":120,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Cliff","descriptions":["The crevice slants back deeply into the face of the cliff and cradles you safely within.  Towards the back, an arched tunnel bores through the rock to the west.  A few animal droppings and a tuft of fur caught on a burr-bush reveal other creatures have sought shelter here as well."],"exits":[{"to":15,"exit":"go","move":"go tunnel"},{"to":13,"exit":"climb","move":"climb down"}]},
  {"id":15,"x":100,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Cliff","descriptions":["The western side of the deep crevice ends abruptly.  Any misstep and it's a long, long fall.  A crumbling ledge above is the only way up -- otherwise, an arched tunnel leads back to the eastern side of the crevice and the alternative route down."],"exits":[{"to":16,"exit":"climb","move":"climb crumbling ledge"},{"to":14,"exit":"go","move":"go tunnel"}]},
  {"id":16,"x":100,"y":-180,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Cliff","descriptions":["Chunks of rock fall with every movement -- this ledge does not appear to be stable at all.  Small spider webs glint within the fracturing stone, creating the illusion of silver threads tying the dark, disintegrating chunks of rock together.  Above, a shallow crevice is an even darker stain upon the black rock."],"exits":[{"to":17,"exit":"climb","move":"climb shallow crevice"},{"to":15,"exit":"climb","move":"climb down"}]},
  {"id":17,"x":100,"y":-200,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Cliff","descriptions":["This shallow crevice offers minimal protection from the wind, and a view, with a hefty dose of vertigo, of the terrain below.  Within the crevice, dark red veins streak the black rock, and gusts of wind blow gritty sand in little swirls.  Above, you can see a round hole in the cliff face."],"exits":[{"to":18,"exit":"climb","move":"climb hole","hidden":true},{"to":16,"exit":"climb","move":"climb down"}]},
  {"id":18,"x":180,"y":80,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Cliff","descriptions":["This large hole is just one climb away from the top of the cliff.  However, very few cracks in the rock are in the right places for holding on, and the wind is especially brisk and strong here.  Some dirty straw tucked within one corner of the hole resembles an untidy nest."],"exits":[{"to":19,"exit":"climb","move":"climb cliff top"},{"to":17,"exit":"climb","move":"climb crevice","hidden":true}]},
  {"id":19,"x":180,"y":60,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Top of Cliff","descriptions":["At the top of the cliff, very little vegetation thrives.  A few scraggly tree-like bushes, with short thick needles, rock in the strong wind gusts, and some grey blotches of lichen stain the dark red rocks.  Jagged basalt boulders litter the top and rise further north in a second cliff, more perilous than the climb below."],"exits":[{"to":20,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":18,"exit":"climb","move":"climb hole"}]},
  {"id":20,"x":160,"y":40,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Cliff Trail","descriptions":["A trail snakes between the barren rocks -- here is a cold and lifeless terrain.  The hiss of wind is constant, the stone hard underfoot.  Grit and sand swirls over the landscape, scratching a forlorn plea in the lonely quiet."],"exits":[{"to":21,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":19,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":21,"x":180,"y":20,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Cliff Trail","descriptions":["A lime-green creeping plant is startling in the barren soil and sand.  Its tiny leaves stand out brightly against the dark ground.  Except for this one patch of green, all else is dark and bare.  The wind thrums along, a constant companion, day and night."],"exits":[{"to":22,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":20,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"}]},
  {"id":22,"x":180,"y":0,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Cliff Trail","descriptions":["Columnar basalt formations, octagonal in shape and in varying heights, rise off to the west.  Arranged like giant steps, the phenomena has a comical appearance, but otherwise it is more rock in a place of rocks."],"exits":[{"to":23,"exit":"northeast","move":"northeast"},{"to":21,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]},
  {"id":23,"x":200,"y":-20,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, High Cliffs","descriptions":["A pile of old bones lies at the base of the high cliffs.  Clearly some animal has scavenged and picked them clean of any identifying features.  A slanting ledge scales up the bluff, although the ascent looks treacherous.  Care and skill are required to prevent the same fatal outcome as the poor creature whose remains are as cold and bare as this land."],"exits":[{"to":22,"exit":"southwest","move":"southwest"},{"to":24,"exit":"climb","move":"climb slanting ledge"}]},
  {"id":24,"x":180,"y":-40,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, High Cliffs","descriptions":["The ledge slants steeply down to the west.  Between the slope and the wind, merely staying in one place is difficult.  A cantilevered ledge overhead, if reachable, appears to be a more practical spot to make decisions about the next stage of the journey."],"exits":[{"to":25,"exit":"climb","move":"climb cantilevered ledge"},{"to":23,"exit":"climb","move":"climb down"}]},
  {"id":25,"x":180,"y":-60,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, High Cliffs","descriptions":["Ice crystal needles fill the cracks in the surface of the ledge.  Cold air sinks from above, yet the sudden chill is unexplainable.  Although the wind gusts are freezing and the height considerable, the year 'round snow of the rim is still far, far above this point.  Closer inspection proves the ice sprouts from within the rock, as the deeper fissures hold larger chunks of ice and frost."],"exits":[{"to":24,"exit":"climb","move":"climb slant ledge"},{"to":26,"exit":"climb","move":"climb wide ledge"}]},
  {"id":26,"x":180,"y":-80,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, High Cliffs","descriptions":["A fine white frost covers all surfaces of the basalt, the red streaks in the rock taking on a pinkish cast beneath the filmy rime.  Patterns splay over the surface like giant snowflakes as the strange ice grows in crystaline formations.  A ledge, slippery with more ice, is visible even further up the cliff."],"exits":[{"to":25,"exit":"climb","move":"climb cantilevered ledge"},{"to":27,"exit":"climb","move":"climb slippery ledge"}]},
  {"id":27,"x":200,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, High Cliffs Ledge","descriptions":["Icicles cling to the crags and fill the clefts in the cliff, with perhaps a single drop of water slowly sliding off to fall below.  Tiny tundra-like mosses grow beneath the icicles' drip, blotching the ledge with yellow-green and red spores from the blooming plants.  Once safely up to this point, one discovers a deep fracture running vertically through the rock.  There does not appear to be any way to climb further up, so the choices at this point are either to descend or attempt to explore the fissure."],"exits":[{"to":28,"exit":"go","move":"go deep fracture"},{"to":26,"exit":"climb","move":"climb wide ledge"}]},
  {"id":28,"x":220,"y":-120,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Geshiger","descriptions":["Daggers of ice drip from the top of a fissure and sparkle as the light beyond strikes the fragile surfaces.  Inside the rock cavity, which drops sharply a few yards forward, the walls, floor and ceiling are all coated with a powdery rimefrost."],"exits":[{"to":29,"exit":"down","move":"down"},{"to":27,"exit":"go","move":"go fissure"}]},
  {"id":29,"x":220,"y":-100,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Geshiger","descriptions":["This cave within the rock is freezing cold!  Ice coats the jagged rock formations with refracting crystals, as if a coarse, heavy snow had blown through.  Powdery slush sloshes underfoot, while a blast of even colder air blows in from around a bend to the northwest."],"exits":[{"to":30,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"},{"to":28,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":30,"x":200,"y":-120,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Geshiger","descriptions":["The cave roof slopes down sharply to meet the ground to the northwest.  In one cramped corner is a narrow slit leading further into the bowels of the rock, the opening crusted with broken fangs of ice."],"exits":[{"to":29,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"},{"to":33,"exit":"go","move":"go narrow slit"}]},
  {"id":31,"x":200,"y":-180,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Geshiger","descriptions":["It's pitch dark and you can't see a thing!","Spears of ice as thick as a 'Tog's arm hang from chunks of rock overhead.  All surfaces are permanently coated in the ice which has taken on a sickeningly bluish tint.  A faint chemical smell, unidentifiable, but most certainly unpleasant, pervades the air."],"exits":[{"to":35,"exit":"east","move":"east"},{"to":32,"exit":"south","move":"south"},{"to":34,"exit":"northwest","move":"northwest"}]},
  {"id":32,"x":200,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Geshiger","descriptions":["It's pitch dark and you can't see a thing!","The walls of the cave are pocked with indentations, grooves and clefts.  Frigid air seeps from them, and the moisture in the air snap freezes to dusty particles of ice.  A faint tinkling must be the sound of that vapor solidifying and falling like glitter dust to the powder-coated floor."],"exits":[{"to":31,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":33,"exit":"climb","move":"climb ice-coated ladder"}]},
  {"id":33,"x":200,"y":-140,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Geshiger","descriptions":["It's pitch dark and you can't see a thing!","Smooth ice veils the cave walls and floor, filling in the cracks and rounding the sharp edges of rock.  An iron ladder affixed to the west wall is also coated in a film of ice and ascends into a dark passage above.  Clumps of ice break from the ceiling above and hit the slick floor below with a loud *crack*."],"exits":[{"to":30,"exit":"up","move":"up"},{"to":32,"exit":"climb","move":"climb ice-coated ladder"}]},
  {"id":34,"x":180,"y":-200,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Geshiger","descriptions":["It's pitch dark and you can't see a thing!","The journey into the rock ends here in a featureless tomb of smooth grey ice.  No rock is visible at all, everything now slicked with the frozen glaze.  Breath freezes instantly with each exhalation in a tiny explosion of icy sparks."],"exits":[{"to":31,"exit":"southeast","move":"southeast"}]},
  {"id":35,"x":220,"y":-180,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Geshiger","descriptions":["It's pitch dark and you can't see a thing!","Frost-shattered rock, sprinkled with powdery white crystals, litters the floor.  The walls are crumbling from the freeze and thaw of moisture that threads through the network of fractures.  A steady melting of ice from within the rock slides down the frozen walls and trickles thinly down a slope deeper into the cavern.  In patches, the rivulet has refrozen into ice slicks likely to send the unwary sliding into the dark below."],"exits":[{"to":31,"exit":"west","move":"west"},{"to":36,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":36,"x":220,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Geshiger","descriptions":["It's pitch dark and you can't see a thing!","Water oozes down the slope of the cave's floor, most of it refrozen into an icy slide.  A chuckle of water spilling over rock resounds through the air, but the source of it out of sight.  The northern wall is a solid, smooth surface of dark red rock splattered with a craze of frost."],"exits":[{"to":35,"exit":"up","move":"up"},{"to":37,"exit":"down","move":"down"}]},
  {"id":37,"x":240,"y":-160,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Geshiger","descriptions":["It's pitch dark and you can't see a thing!","Enough water collected here at one time to cover the floor and has since frozen into a solid pool of ice.  Smooth as a mirror, it reflects light with a sparkle.  The icy pattern of frost creeps over the walls in a swirling design, but the bitter cold and pervasive dark beyond belies the beauty of ice and rock."],"exits":[{"to":38,"exit":"north","move":"north"},{"to":36,"exit":"up","move":"up"}]},
  {"id":38,"x":240,"y":-180,"z":0,"title":"Aesry Surlaenis'a, Geshiger","descriptions":["It's pitch dark and you can't see a thing!","A niche at the far end of the wall is filled with the powdery frost.  Thin wires run over the opening like a web, and icicles dangle from the wires in a scalloped formation.  A cold, cold wind gushes up from cracks in the floor making it difficult to get enough breath to speak."],"exits":[{"to":37,"exit":"south","move":"south"}]}
 ],
 "labels": [
  {"text":"Yvhh La'tami","x":-10,"y":-60,"z":0},
  {"text":"Yvhh La'tami","x":190,"y":0,"z":0},
  {"text":"Snaer Hafwa","x":190,"y":-210,"z":0}
 ]
}
